  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math> are non-zero real numbers and if the system of equations&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></math> have a non-trivial solution, then <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
